-- title:
--   Unique extension of automorphisms along a constant field change
-- statement:
--   Let $K_0$ and $K$ be fields, $\varphi\colon K_0\to K$ a ring homomorphism, and $\Gamma$ a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$. For a field $L$, write $\bar F_L$ for [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC L Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the set of those Laurent series of the form `intSeriesC L pf / intSeriesC L pg`, where $k\in\mathbb{Z}$, $f$ and $g$ are modular forms of weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb{R})$, $p_f,p_g$ are power series over $\mathbb{Z}$ satisfying the predicate `IsIntegralQExp` with respect to $f$ and to $g$ respectively, and `intSeriesC L pg ≠ 0`. Let `coeffMap` $\varphi\colon K_0((q))\to K((q))$ be the ring homomorphism applying $\varphi$ to each coefficient. Given a $K_0$-algebra automorphism $\sigma_0$ of $\bar F_{K_0}$, the assertion is that there is exactly one $K$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\bar F_K$ with the following compatibility: whenever $x_0\in\bar F_{K_0}$ and $x\in\bar F_K$ have underlying Laurent series related by $x = (\mathrm{coeffMap}\,\varphi)(x_0)$, then $\sigma(x) = (\mathrm{coeffMap}\,\varphi)(\sigma_0(x_0))$ as Laurent series over $K$.
--
--   This is the function-field base-change statement that automorphisms over the field of constants extend uniquely after enlarging the constants, the relevant linear disjointness here being that of $K$ and $K_0((q))$ over $K_0$ inside $K((q))$. It is used to transport automorphisms of the $q$-expansion function field of a modular curve along coefficient maps, for instance in the comparison of fibres of the $q$-expansion map for the groups $\Gamma_H$ and in the construction of diamond operators on reductions of the function field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_existsUnique_algEquiv_qExpFunctionFieldC_coe_apply_eq_coeffMap.lean

